From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Jorge Ramirez-Ortiz <jorge.ramirez@oss.qualcomm.com>
Date: Thu, 11 Jun 2026 00:00:00 +0200
Subject: [PATCH] arm64: dts: qcom: kodiak-el2: fix DSP firmware-name; add venus
 SMMU streams (WIP)

The base RB3Gen2 DTS sets the adsp/cdsp remoteproc firmware-name to
"qcom/qcs6490/<x>.mbn".  linux-firmware ships the RB3Gen2 DSP images
under qcom/qcm6490/, so the PAS driver's request_firmware() fails with
-ENOENT and the remoteproc never reaches the OP-TEE PAS authenticate/
reset step (so it looks like the kernel "never calls OP-TEE for PAS").

Override the adsp/cdsp firmware-name to qcom/qcm6490/ in the EL2 overlay
so the images are found and PAS-over-OP-TEE proceeds.

The kodiak EL2 overlay already enables &venus (status = "okay") and the
video-firmware subnode upstream.  Add the second apps_smmu stream mapping
to &venus required to boot the codec over the PAS/OP-TEE firmware path;
the base kodiak.dtsi only declares the first (0x2180) stream.

WARNING: UNDER DEVELOPMENT.  The &venus enablement is experimental and
not yet validated on Kodiak.  The IOMMU stream IDs and the firmware-
loading path are still being worked out; expect this hunk to change.

Signed-off-by: Jorge Ramirez-Ortiz <jorge.ramirez@oss.qualcomm.com>
---
diff --git a/arch/arm64/boot/dts/qcom/kodiak-el2.dtso b/arch/arm64/boot/dts/qcom/kodiak-el2.dtso
index fd000fc57..4e72e6982 100644
--- a/arch/arm64/boot/dts/qcom/kodiak-el2.dtso
+++ b/arch/arm64/boot/dts/qcom/kodiak-el2.dtso
@@ -13,10 +13,18 @@ &gpu_zap_shader {
 };

 &remoteproc_adsp {
+	/*
+	 * The base RB3Gen2 DTS firmware-name points at qcom/qcs6490, which
+	 * carries no flat adsp.mbn; the RB3Gen2 firmware namespace is qcm6490.
+	 * Without this the PAS driver's request_firmware() fails with -ENOENT
+	 * and the remoteproc never reaches the OP-TEE PAS authenticate step.
+	 */
+	firmware-name = "qcom/qcm6490/adsp.mbn";
 	iommus = <&apps_smmu 0x1800 0x0>;
 };

 &remoteproc_cdsp {
+	firmware-name = "qcom/qcm6490/cdsp.mbn";
 	iommus = <&apps_smmu 0x11a0 0x0400>;
 };

@@ -37,6 +45,9 @@ wlan_ce_mem: wlan-ce@4cd000 {
 &venus {
 	status = "okay";

+	iommus = <&apps_smmu 0x2180 0x20>,
+		 <&apps_smmu 0x2184 0x20>;
+
 	video-firmware {
 		iommus = <&apps_smmu 0x21a2 0x0>;
 	};
--
2.34.1
